ision-making, teamwork/communication, professional development.\n\nWe need to weigh strengths vs weaknesses. For long-distance flights, reliability, decision-making, stress handling, teamwork, communication are crucial. Also health (eating unhealthily) could affect long flights.\n\nCandidate A: strong anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. Weakness: unfriendly (teamwork), unhealthy eating (health). Leadership good, but unfriendly may affect crew cooperation. Health could be issue for long flights.\n\nCandidate B: conscientious, stress handling, weather assessment, computer skills. Weakness: pretentious, wrong tone. Communication tone could affect crew. But overall strong technical and stress.\n\nCandidate C: quick correct decisions, concern for others, attention skills. Weakness: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. Egocentric and communication issues could harm teamwork. Lack of professional development.\n\nCandidate D: responds adequately to unexpected events, concentration, problem solving, responsibility. Weakness: moody, loner. Moodiness could affect crew; loner may affect teamwork.\n\nWe need provisional preference. Which candidate seems best overall? B has strong stress handling, weather assessment (critical), conscientiousness, computer skills. Communication tone issue but maybe manageable. A has strong anticipation and leadership but health and unfriendly. D has strong problem solving and responsibility but moodiness and loner. C has quick decisions and concern for others but communication and egocentric.\n\nProbably B is best overall, as strengths align with technical competence, stress handling, reliability, and weaknesses are more about attitude but less severe than health or moodiness? Pretentiousness and tone could affect crew but maybe less critical than health issues.\n\nThus provisional preference: Candidate B.\n\nWe need to note uncertainties: we lack info on actual teamwork performance, health status beyond eating, actual flight experience, etc. Also we don't know other agents' info that could shift.\n\nWhat would change vote: If other agents have strong positive evidence for another candidate (e.g., D's teamwork, A's health, C's willingness to improve) or negative evidence for B (e.g., serious communication failures), we would reconsider.\n\nNow produce output.\n\nPUBLIC_MESSAGE: include current position (Candidate B), summarize key evidence (list positives and negatives), mention evidence from others (none yet), major alternatives (A, D, C), tradeoff (B's attitude vs A's health, D's moodiness, C's communication), remaining uncertainty (lack of data on actual crew interaction, health impact, etc.), what would change vote (strong positive evidence for others or negative for B).\n\nMETADATA_JSON: vote \"Candidate B\"."}
